      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Mixed decimal expressions follow the usual order: evaluate parentheses first, then multiplication and division from left to right, then addition and subtraction from left to right. Do not add terms before completing a higher-priority operation unless parentheses require it.\n\nFor 12.28 × 1.5 − 36 ÷ 2.4, calculate the product and quotient first: 18.42 − 15 = 3.42. A common error is to subtract before dividing, which changes the expression's meaning.",
